# The actions /sbin/privd runs. In the sealed base at
# /usr/share/slopos/privd/actions; the grammar is slopos_priv_core::policy's.
#
# Every mechanism runs as uid 0, or as its requester, with no more than its
# action names. Whoever may ask for an action is listed in order, and the first
# line whose principal matches the requester decides, at its level; a person no
# line matches is answered by an administrator's password where an admin line
# stands.
#
# What a person reads is held to slopos_priv_core::words: describe completes
# "{App} wants to ...", detail says what follows from allowing it, and verb
# names the button that allows it.

action org.slopos.power.poweroff
  program  /bin/halt
  args     halt
  args     poweroff
  args     shutdown
  caps     Power
  uid      0
  allow    root
  allow    greeter alone
  allow    user alone
  allow    admin
  allow    paired
  describe "power off the computer"
  detail   "Anything that isn't saved will be lost."
  verb     "Power off"

action org.slopos.power.reboot
